  "brief": "Enghouse Systems is acquiring MIND CTI for $25.4 million in an all-cash transaction.\n\nEnghouse Systems / MIND CTI (Announced): Enghouse Systems to Acquire MIND CTI. Enghouse Systems is acquiring MIND CTI for $25.4 million in an all-cash transaction [4, 5]. The acquisition was announced by MIND CTI and Enghouse Systems [1, 2, 3]. The deal is expected to be completed in the future [1, 2, 3].\nNaver Financial / Dunamu (Pending approval): Naver Financial and Dunamu Deal. Naver Financial and Dunamu are awaiting approval from South Korea's FTC [6, 7, 8]. The deal is currently under review by the FTC [6, 7, 8].\nRubico / another Two Newbuilding MR Tankers (Announced): Rubico Acquires Two Newbuilding MR Tankers. Rubico has announced the acquisition of two newbuilding MR tankers [9, 10]. The deal is expected to increase Rubico's potential gross revenue backlog to about $523 million [9]. No further information is available on the deal at this time [10].\nEnghouse Systems / MIND C.T.I. (Announced): Enghouse Systems Acquires MIND C.T.I. Enghouse Systems is acquiring MIND C.T.I. in an all-cash transaction [12, 11]. The deal is valued at $25.4 million [11]. The acquisition is expected to expand Enghouse Systems' telecom and enterprise communications software offerings [11].\nWilliams / Momentum Midstream (Announced): Williams to Buy Momentum Midstream. Williams is buying Momentum Midstream for $5.5 Billion [13, 14]. The deal was announced by Williams [13]. No further information is available [13].\nICP / R.M. Lucas Roofing Brand (Announced): ICP Acquires R.M. Lucas Roofing Brand. ICP has acquired the R.M. Lucas Roofing Brand [15]. The deal was announced [15].\nArgenx / UNP (Announced): Argenx to Acquire UNP. Argenx is acquiring UNP, a peptide platform, in a deal worth up to $1.15 billion [16, 17, 18]. The deal is expected to advance next-generation medicines [19]. The acquisition was announced and no further details have been released [17].\nCribl / Tero (Announced): Cribl Buys Tero. Cribl is acquiring Tero in its third deal in four months [20]. The deal was announced by Cribl [20].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- A Vesuvius shareholder is pushing for the company to provide RHI with due diligence [21].\n- Softbank and ABB are reentering talks after China blocked their acquisition [22].\n- A fake private equity executive has been convicted over a bid to pump shares [23].",
